From 9d34e6ccf16a5ad797e768e4e20682bffc3ddc06 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 16:48:55 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] fix(approval): a refused approval tells the agent not to work
 around it and to ask the user

A denied, timed-out or withdrawn approval, a smart approval block, a hard rule, a deny rule, a hardline block, an unattended refusal, a plugin approval, a protected write, an MCP trust denial and a failed review told the agent only "do not retry", in different words. Some said nothing about what to do instead.

Every such result now ends with one instruction (tools/approval_guidance.py): do not work around the block (no other tool, script, rephrased command, or smaller steps to the same outcome), and if the action is still needed ask the user for explicit authorization with the clarify tool (in the reply when clarify is unavailable; a subagent's question goes to its parent chat through the existing subagent question path), stating the exact action, why it is needed and the checker's reason, then wait. A hard rule, a deny rule and a hardline block say an answer in the chat does not clear them and the user can run the action outside the agent or change the rule. The checker's rule name and reason are named in the message, once.

The user's clarify answer is already the user's own words in the smart approval review, so the same action then runs without a second card; a test covers the loop.

No new config key.
